# Manual REST Client requests for GET and PUT /cancellation-rules (VS Code REST Client).
# Sign in with an approved review account of REVIEW_ACCOUNTS in apps/backend/.env: set the email and code below.
# Codes are read from the backend log when RESEND_API_KEY is unset.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = admin@example.com
@code = 345678

### Request a sign-in code (expects 202)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "locale": "pt-BR"
}

### Sign in (expects 200 with accessToken)
# @name session
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{code}}"
}

###
### Read both rules (expects 200 with { surf, skate }, each text or null; any approved account)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Save the surf rule (expects 200 with both rules, the text trimmed; admins only). Saving a different text clears the deadlines of the upcoming surf classes
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules/surf
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "O aluno pode cancelar até 12 horas antes do início da aula."
}

### Unknown discipline (expects 422 cancellationRule.discipline.invalid)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules/kitesurf
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "x"
}

### Blank text (expects 422 cancellationRule.text.required)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules/skate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "   "
}

### More than 2000 characters (expects 422 cancellationRule.text.max.length): repeat a long text

### Without a token (expects 401 auth.token.invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules

### As a student or instructor (expects 403 user.role.notAdmin on PUT): use that account's token
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cancellation-rules/surf
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "x"
}
